I was hopeless

503
00:40:25,135 --> 00:40:26,535
it was stinging

504
00:40:26,535 --> 00:40:27,935
running roadless

505
00:40:27,935 --> 00:40:30,335
we were singing at the top of our lungs to the numbness

506
00:40:30,335 --> 00:40:34,035
this city never died

507
00:40:35,035 --> 00:40:37,535
What was the root of it all? Huh, I couldn't say

508
00:40:37,535 --> 00:40:40,135
Used to jump and then fall, rugged and cliché

509
00:40:40,135 --> 00:40:42,735
Would shrug it off without complaint, not a sound

510
00:40:42,735 --> 00:40:45,635
No use in trying to find friends, 'cause in the end nobody sticks around

511
00:40:45,635 --> 00:40:48,435
It's when you shoved yourself into a crowded place

512
00:40:48,435 --> 00:40:51,135
That you turned around and found yourself in love in outer space

513
00:40:51,135 --> 00:40:53,935
Cue the reckless nights, no strings, laughing at our own dreams

514
00:40:53,935 --> 00:40:55,935
Just what the hell was so funny?

515
00:40:55,935 --> 00:40:58,635
Bark up the wrong tree, stumble, used to falling great heights

516
00:40:58,635 --> 00:41:01,135
Amidst a concrete jungle, singing 'cause it felt right

517
00:41:01,135 --> 00:41:03,835
We mixed the ennui and troubles, rhyming our discontent

518
00:41:03,835 --> 00:41:06,735
And though it's history, I can't forget the time that we spent

519
00:41:06,735 --> 00:41:09,335
Convinced that this could mean another end exists between real and pretend

520
00:41:09,335 --> 00:41:12,335
A twisted alter-fiction where I missed my chance, did not ascend, and

521
00:41:12,335 --> 00:41:15,535
Disappearing into the mist of never happened, is the me that I can never befriend

522
00:41:15,635 --> 00:41:17,835
I let it go

523
00:41:17,935 --> 00:41:21,235
Fade in, fade out

524
00:41:21,235 --> 00:41:24,135
this crazy dream

525
00:41:24,135 --> 00:41:26,835
Without a direction,

526
00:41:26,835 --> 00:41:29,335
floating aimlessly

527
00:41:29,335 --> 00:41:33,735
There's nothing left back there for me

528
00:41:34,735 --> 00:41:39,135
Breathe in, but it won't stop the rain from pouring

529
00:41:39,135 --> 00:41:43,835
We'd run right through

530
00:41:43,835 --> 00:41:46,135
those nights

531
00:41:46,135 --> 00:41:49,435
I'll never find my way back to you inside this labyrinth of lights

532
00:41:49,435 --> 00:41:51,735
There was madness in the meaning

533
00:41:51,735 --> 00:41:53,535
never laugh less

534
00:41:53,535 --> 00:41:56,235
we were screaming at the top of our lungs to the numbness

535
00:41:56,235 --> 00:41:58,735
this city never died

536
00:41:58,735 --> 00:42:01,135
But was there ever a soul inside?

537
00:42:01,135 --> 00:42:03,635
Chasing fireflies between the soaring high-rises

538
00:42:03,635 --> 00:42:06,235
Left a trail behind, defined it, wasted time of our lives

539
00:42:06,235 --> 00:42:08,935
Silent singer, overworked and underpaid

540
00:42:08,935 --> 00:42:11,435
Thinks an office is a coffin until off is where you're laid

541
00:42:11,435 --> 00:42:13,935
Yet a thought persists, an optimist who ought to be afraid

542
00:42:13,935 --> 00:42:16,635
Saw the nothing wrong in writing songs behind the lonely shade

543
00:42:16,635 --> 00:42:19,135
Is the world a sadder place without the words that you conveyed?

544
00:42:19,135 --> 00:42:21,735
When the ladder fell and shattered every bar that we had played?

545
00:42:21,735 --> 00:42:24,535
Does it matter in the end the sound diminished and decayed

546
00:42:24,535 --> 00:42:27,335
And your friends grew tired of fantasy, you're wishing they had stayed?

547
00:42:27,335 --> 00:42:30,035
You don't get to say I miss you, you watched your heroes fade

548
00:42:30,035 --> 00:42:32,635
Into the rear view mirror of the villain you portrayed
into the rearview mirror of the villain you portrayed.

549
00:42:32,635 --> 00:42:35,135
Stop the pity party, listen, you don't get to be dismayed

550
00:42:35,135 --> 00:42:37,635
You don't get to be emotional, feel blessed you got it made

551
00:42:37,635 --> 00:42:40,135
These the best of years of life because you chose to make a trade

552
00:42:40,135 --> 00:42:42,735
Recollect the days you hoped and you prayed for this

553
00:42:42,735 --> 00:42:44,435
What is there to miss?

554
00:42:44,535 --> 00:42:47,535
Fade in, fade out

555
00:42:47,535 --> 00:42:50,235
this hazy dream

556
00:42:50,235 --> 00:42:52,935
Without a direction,

557
00:42:52,935 --> 00:42:55,435
roaming aimlessly

558
00:42:55,435 --> 00:42:59,835
There's nothing left back there for me

559
00:43:00,035 --> 00:43:04,635
Pretend it's the end of a made-up story

560
00:43:04,735 --> 00:43:09,735
I'll fly, no proof

561
00:43:09,735 --> 00:43:11,835
those heights

562
00:43:11,835 --> 00:43:15,235
I'll never find another chance to say, hey, thanks for saving my life

563
00:43:15,235 --> 00:43:16,635
I was hopeless

564
00:43:16,635 --> 00:43:17,935
it was stinging

565
00:43:17,935 --> 00:43:19,235
driving roadless

566
00:43:19,235 --> 00:43:21,635
we were singing at the top of our lungs to the numbness

567
00:43:21,635 --> 00:43:24,235
this city never died

568
00:43:24,235 --> 00:43:26,735
I'll say goodbye to the soul inside

569
00:43:26,735 --> 00:43:29,035
And yet somehow, there was romance

570
00:43:29,035 --> 00:43:31,635
in our self-hate, we've got no chance

571
00:43:31,635 --> 00:43:34,235
in this light maze, but let's hold hands

572
00:43:34,235 --> 00:43:36,735
through the night haze, we'll run so fast

573
00:43:36,735 --> 00:43:39,235
'til the school chime, 'til the train runs

574
00:43:39,235 --> 00:43:41,735
We know it's time, we're the sane ones

575
00:43:41,735 --> 00:43:44,435
Waking up now, to the real life

576
00:43:44,435 --> 00:43:47,235
Let me daydream, 'til the next night

577
00:43:47,235 --> 00:43:49,235
I'll keep waiting

578
00:43:49,735 --> 00:43:54,235
I'll keep waiting for you

579
00:44:18,235 --> 00:44:21,235
Waking up now, to my real life

580
00:44:21,235 --> 00:44:23,935
let me daydream, 'til the next flight

581
00:44:23,935 --> 00:44:26,735
Drowning so long, I got older

582
00:44:26,735 --> 00:44:29,235
now the crowd's gone, is it over?

583
00:44:29,235 --> 00:44:31,735
Is it over?

